5. Simplified the window.matchMedia mock
6. Added proper session mock for SessionProvider
7. Kept the core component structure but removed Jest dependencies

The main change is removing all Jest-related code and replacing it with standard JavaScript module mocking. This should resolve the "jest is not defined" error while still providing the necessary mocked functionality for the component to work.

The mock implementations are now done through regular objects and functions, which should work in any JavaScript environment without requiring Jest. The component structure remains the same, but the mocking approach has been simplified and made more compatible with the runtime environment.

